# UI-MINIMAP-1 C: the minimap's controls at 1024 x 768 (docs/re/ui.md 2.9 Q6). A left press on the
# diamond centres the camera on the clicked world point (AnnoFrame 0x100029f0, turn 0, the minimap
# zoom window); the top-right + and - zoom the minimap (command 0x1b, the view box grows and
# shrinks); the magnifier's + and - step the main zoom one built level (commands 0xa / 9); the
# chevrons are dead until VIEW-TURN-1; a press on the parchment outside the diamond, also on its
# strip left of the chrome (x 765..778), is the UI's and reaches no map action.
# lan5 is 1431 x 1431 tiles. (900, 50) is (135, 38) from the wrapper's (765, 12): X = 129 * 1.03,
# Y = 38 * 1.03, D = X - 128 = 4.87, P = 83.15, Q = 73.41 -> tile (trunc(1431 * 73.41 / 256),
# trunc(1431 * 83.15 / 256)) = (410, 464) through the whole window (z = 1).
# Launch: --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
expect fact minimap.clicks == 0
expect fact minimap.zoom == 100
expect fact camera.pans == 0
expect fact camera.tile.x != 410
# The diamond: the camera jumps there, no pan, no selection click.
click_px 900 50
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.clicks == 1
expect fact camera.tile.x >= 409
expect fact camera.tile.x <= 411
expect fact camera.tile.y >= 463
expect fact camera.tile.y <= 465
expect fact camera.pans == 0
expect fact selection.clicks == 0
# The parchment outside the diamond, on the strip left of the chrome (770, 30): (5, 18) from the
# wrapper, dx = -123 < -36: taken, nothing moves. A drag from there starts no pan either.
click_px 770 30
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.clicks == 1
expect fact selection.clicks == 0
expect fact camera.pans == 0
expect fact camera.tile.x >= 409
expect fact camera.tile.x <= 411
ldrag_px 772 20 600 300
wait frames 3
expect fact camera.pans == 0
expect fact camera.tile.x >= 409
expect fact camera.tile.x <= 411
# The same strip inside the diamond (770, 76): (5, 64), dx = -123 >= -128: the camera jumps to
# the diamond's left corner, the world's far x and near y (X = -1 * 1.03, D = -129.03, P = 2.81,
# Q = 260.87 -> (1458, 15), past the world's x; the view's clamp to the scene's bounds then
# keeps the camera inside its screen rectangle, at about (1209, 265) on lan5).
click_px 770 76
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.clicks == 2
expect fact camera.tile.x >= 1204
expect fact camera.tile.x <= 1214
expect fact camera.tile.y >= 260
expect fact camera.tile.y <= 270
expect fact selection.clicks == 0
expect fact camera.pans == 0
# The top-right + (959, 7) 19 x 21 and - (982, 19): the minimap zoom 1.0 -> 0.85 -> 0.7 and back;
# the view box grows by 1 / z and returns (at level 2 of a 1431-tile world 1.361 * 4 * 2200 /
# 1431 * 0.972 = 8.1 px across at z = 1, 11.6 px at 0.7: 9 and 13 pixels drawn).
expect fact minimap.box.w == 9
click_px 968 17
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.zoom == 85
click_px 968 17
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.zoom == 70
expect fact minimap.box.w == 13
click_px 991 29
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.zoom == 85
click_px 991 29
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.zoom == 100
expect fact minimap.box.w == 9
click_px 991 29
wait frames 3
expect fact minimap.zoom == 100
expect fact minimap.clicks == 2
# The magnifier's + (796, 135) and - (826, 153), 19 x 21: one built level per press (tile widths
# 20 -> 42 -> 84, clamped at level 0), then back.
expect fact view.tile_w == 20
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 42
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 84
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 84
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 42
# The chevrons (965, 140) and (986, 140), 19 x 31: taken, nothing turns (VIEW-TURN-1).
click_px 974 155
wait frames 3
click_px 995 155
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 42
expect fact minimap.zoom == 100
expect fact minimap.clicks == 2
expect fact selection.clicks == 0
expect fact camera.pans == 0
quit
